\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Theorem}
\title{A long symmetric torus is recovered at every site}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{On the periodic cubical torus with both directions of every
axis and with every weight equal to #{1}, let #{N\ge 3}. Every
vertex is a \vocabk{recovery site}{fdip-00PQ} of rank #{d}. For #{N=1} every
difference of a function is zero, so the affine functions do
not span a free module of positive rank. For #{N=2} the vertex
#{x-\varepsilon_i} equals #{x+\varepsilon_i}, and a constant
difference on that axis exists only when #{2a_i=0}. The
forward-edge torus has no backward edge, so the two directions
required by the \vocabk{recovery site}{fdip-00PQ} are not both
present. This is the obstruction of \ref{fdip-00PE}. If one outgoing edge at a
vertex #{x} is deleted, the out-degree at #{x} is one less
than the out-degree at a vertex that still has every edge, so
the rank is not constant on any set containing both vertices.}

\proof{
\p{Since #{N\ge 3}, the vertices within two steps of #{x} are
distinct and form a coordinate patch that embeds in the torus.
On that patch the function #{f(y)=\sum_i a_i(\tilde y_i-\tilde
x_i)} has every prescribed difference #{a_i\in k}. The odd
vectors of \ref{fdip-00PO} are therefore hit, and they form a
free basis of rank #{d}. Every weight is #{1}, a unit, so
#{\bar q} is the standard dot form and \ref{fdip-00PC} gives
nondegeneracy. The two directions are present and the weights
agree. \ref{fdip-00PK} supplies the commutator square on the
cells of the patch. Thus every vertex is a recovery site of
rank #{d}.}

\p{For #{N=1} there is one vertex, and #{f(x+\varepsilon_i)-f(x)
=0}. For #{N=2} the two steps #{+\varepsilon_i} and
#{-\varepsilon_i} are the same vertex, so summing the
difference around the axis yields #{2a_i=0}. On the
forward-edge torus the backward generator is absent, so no odd
vector is defined. Deleting one outgoing edge lowers the
out-degree by one at its source and leaves some other vertex
at out-degree #{2d}, so the ranks differ.}
}
